      "title": "Props, State and One-Way Flow",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Props, State and One-Way Flow",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Props vs State",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Props",
                "State"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Owner",
                  "Parent",
                  "The component"
                ],
                [
                  "Mutable?",
                  "{red:Read-only}",
                  "Via setter only"
                ],
                [
                  "Change means",
                  "New input",
                  "==Re-render=="
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. One-Way Flow",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Parent state",
                    "sub": "useState",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Props down",
                    "sub": "read-only",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Child",
                    "sub": "renders",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Callback up",
                    "sub": "onAdd()",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const [n, setN] = useState(0);",
                "<Child n={n} onAdd={() => setN(c => c + 1)} />"
              ],
              "note": "data down as n, event up as onAdd"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==UI = f(props, state)==",
                "A re-render re-runs the function with **new values**"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Derive, Don't Store",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Derivable from props or other state? ==Compute it in render==",
                "Stored copies drift out of sync"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never mutate props",
              "text": "The child asks the parent through a ==callback prop=="
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Props vs state?** Props are read-only input; state is owned and triggers re-renders.",
                "**How does a child change parent data?** It calls a callback prop."
              ],
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "useState and Immutable Updates",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "useState and Immutable Updates",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Hook and Snapshots",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`const [value, setValue] = useState(initial)` → ==current value== + ==setter==",
                "`initial` is used ==only on the first render==",
                "Setter call ==schedules a re-render==",
                "State is a **snapshot**: the variable keeps its old value in this render"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Updater Form",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "New value depends on the previous one → pass `c => c + 1`",
                "Avoids {red:stale values} in batched updates"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "setCount(count + 1);",
                "setCount(count + 1); // +1 total",
                "setCount(c => c + 1);",
                "setCount(c => c + 1); // +2 total"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Immutable Updates",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "React compares with ==Object.is==",
                "A mutated object keeps its reference → {red:no re-render}"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Goal",
                "Pattern"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Object",
                  "`{...obj, key: v}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Add",
                  "`[...arr, item]`"
                ],
                [
                  "Remove",
                  "`arr.filter(x => x.id !== id)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Edit",
                  "`arr.map(x => x.id === id ? {...x, done: true} : x)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Replace, never mutate",
              "text": "Build a ==new== object or array, then pass it to the setter."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Lifting State Up",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Lifting State Up",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Lift to the Common Parent",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Siblings need the same data: move the state to their ==closest common parent==",
                "Parent passes the {blue:value} as a prop and a {purple:setter} as a callback prop",
                "Child calls the callback; the parent stays the ==single source of truth=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Child event",
                    "sub": "calls callback",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Parent setState",
                    "sub": "owns state",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Re-render",
                    "sub": "new props down",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Value Down, Callback Up",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "function Parent() {",
                "  const [temp, setTemp] = useState('');",
                "  return <>",
                "    <Input value={temp} onChange={setTemp} />",
                "    <Display value={temp} />",
                "  </>;",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "both siblings read one state"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes and Limits",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`useState(props.value)` in a child: the copy ==ignores later prop changes==",
                "Use the prop directly; keep no second copy"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Situation",
                "Reach for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Props pass through many layers",
                  "==Context== or composition"
                ],
                [
                  "Only one component uses it",
                  "Local `useState`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "One owner for the state. Props **down**, events **up**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Controlled vs Uncontrolled Inputs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Controlled vs Uncontrolled Inputs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Who Holds the Value",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Controlled}: `value` + `onChange` bound to state",
                "==React is the source of truth== for the field"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "<input value={v}",
                " onChange={e => setV(e.target.value)} />"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Uncontrolled}: the ==DOM holds the value==",
                "Read it with `ref.current.value`, or on submit via `FormData`",
                "Set the initial value with `defaultValue`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which to Use",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Controlled",
                "Uncontrolled"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Value lives in",
                  "React state",
                  "The DOM"
                ],
                [
                  "Suits",
                  "Live validation, formatting, disabling submit",
                  "Simple forms, **file inputs**"
                ],
                [
                  "Initial value",
                  "`useState('')`",
                  "`defaultValue`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`value` without `onChange` makes the field ==read-only== and logs a warning",
                "`undefined` to a defined value flips uncontrolled to controlled"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Initialise to ''",
              "text": "Start state as `''`, never `undefined`, so the input never switches mode."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Context Basics",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Context Basics",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Provider and Consumer",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`createContext(default)` makes the context",
                "`useContext(Ctx)` gives the ==nearest Provider== value above",
                "The ==default== applies only when **no Provider** is above"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const ThemeCtx = createContext(\"light\");",
                "<ThemeCtx.Provider value={theme}>",
                "  <App />",
                "</ThemeCtx.Provider>",
                "const theme = useContext(ThemeCtx);"
              ],
              "note": "no props passed through the layers between"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. State and Re-renders",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Context is ==not state==: keep `useState` or `useReducer` in the Provider",
                "Put the **value and setter** in the context",
                "Consumers all re-render when the value changes **by reference**",
                "Memoise object values with `useMemo`, or ==split contexts=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "jsx",
              "lines": [
                "const [theme, setTheme] = useState(\"light\");",
                "const value = useMemo(",
                "  () => ({ theme, setTheme }), [theme]);",
                "return <ThemeCtx.Provider value={value}>"
              ],
              "note": "stable object until theme changes"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Good fit",
                "Poor fit"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Theme",
                  "Form input"
                ],
                [
                  "Current user",
                  "Mouse position"
                ],
                [
                  "Locale",
                  "Rapidly changing data"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Inline `value={{ a, b }}` re-renders every consumer."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Fix prop drilling?** Provider above, `useContext` below",
                "**No Provider?** The default value",
                "**Why useMemo?** A new object re-renders every consumer"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "State and Data Flow Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "State and Data Flow Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Flow and Setters",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Props go ==down==, events go ==up== as callback props",
                "Props are {red:read-only}; state is **owned**, and a change triggers a re-render",
                "State is a ==snapshot== per render: the variable keeps its old value after `setX`",
                "Depends on previous state? Use the updater: `setN(n => n + 1)`",
                "==Replace==, never mutate: same reference means no re-render"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Immutable Cheats",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Do",
                "Pattern"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Update object",
                  "`{...obj, key: v}`"
                ],
                [
                  "Add",
                  "`[...arr, x]`"
                ],
                [
                  "Remove",
                  "`arr.filter(x => x.id !== id)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Edit",
                  "`arr.map(x => x.id === id ? {...x, done: true} : x)`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Where State Lives",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "One component",
                    "sub": "local `useState`",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Siblings",
                    "sub": "lift to common parent",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Many distant consumers",
                    "sub": "context",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Inputs",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Controlled",
                "Uncontrolled"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Source of truth",
                  "React state",
                  "The DOM"
                ],
                [
                  "Wiring",
                  "`value` + `onChange`",
                  "`ref` / `defaultValue`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never switch modes",
              "text": "Initialise state to `''`, not undefined. Going from undefined to a value flips the input from uncontrolled to controlled."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Count is 0. One click runs `setN(n + 1)` three times. What is n after the re-render?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "**1**, not 3",
                "State is a snapshot: all three calls set 0 + 1",
                "`setN(c => c + 1)` three times gives 3"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "`todos.push(t); setTodos(todos)` never updates the list. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Same array reference, so `Object.is` sees no change",
                "Fix: `setTodos([...todos, t])`"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A child does `useState(props.value)`. The parent later passes a new value. What does the child show?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The old value",
                "The initial value is used only on the first render, so the copy goes stale",
                "Use the prop directly, or lift the state"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
